            "result_text": "Perfect! I've created the regex pattern and saved it to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nThe regex works as follows:\n\n1. **Line start with IPv4 check**: `^(?=.*\\b...\\b)` - Ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address using lookahead\n2. **IPv4 pattern**: Matches each octet as 0-255 without leading zeros (e.g., `192` matches, but `01` or `001` don't)\n3. **Date capture with proper ranges**:\n   - Months 01,03,05,07,08,10,12: days 01-31\n   - Months 04,06,09,11: days 01-30  \n   - February: days 01-29\n4. **Last date matching**: The negative lookahead `(?![^\\n]*\\bDATE\\b)` ensures no other date follows on the same line\n5. **Word boundaries**: `\\b` around dates and IPv4 prevent partial matches and false positives like \"user1134-12-1234\"\n\nWhen used with `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`, it will return only the captured date strings from lines containing IPv4 addresses."
